# Project Structure

Split frontend and backend in one repository. Specs in `features/` are the source of truth.

## Directory Layout
```
oc-vehicle-reservations/
  features/                  # SDD specs
  frontend/                  # Vue 3 + Vite + Vuetify 4
    public/                  # .htaccess for SPA deploy
    src/
      views/                 # Route-level pages
      components/            # Reusable UI (forms, nav, dialogs)
        layout/              # Page shells: PageShell, SectionCard, DetailHeader, DetailLayout (see ui-style-system.mdc)
        common/              # ListState, ComingSoon, ConfirmModal/ConfirmProvider
      services/              # Axios API modules (*Services.js)
      composables/           # useRequest, useConfirm, useRoles, …
      models/                # Pure per-entity domain/display helpers (users.js)
      stores/                # Pinia stores (auth.js); index.js creates the Pinia instance
      config/                # utils.js (errorMessage helper)
      utils/                 # Pure helper functions
      plugins/               # vuetify.js, webfontloader.js
      router.js
      main.js
      App.vue
    vite.config.js
    package.json
  backend/                   # Node + Express + Sequelize (ES modules)
    server.js
    app/
      routes/                # Express routers; index.js mounts all
      controllers/           # Request handlers
      models/                # Sequelize models; index.js wires associations
      authorization/         # authenticate, role guards, area-scope helpers
      helpers/               # fields.js (parseId, requiredText), response shapers (users.js)
      config/                # env, db, auth, logger, sequelizeInstance
    scripts/                 # npm-run scripts: make-admin.mjs, seed.mjs
    tests/                   # Jest + supertest; helpers.js, setup.js
    package.json
```

## Naming Conventions
*   Frontend services: `camelCase` + `Services.js` (e.g. `authServices.js`, `areaServices.js`).
*   Backend files: `resource.controller.js`, `resource.routes.js`, `resource.model.js`.
*   Multi-word URL segments: kebab-case (`/vehicle-types`).

## Environment Variables
Backend (`backend/.env`, falling back to the repo-root `.env`; see `app/config/env.js`):
*   `DB_HOST`, `DB_USER`, `DB_PW`, `DB_NAME` — MySQL connection (default database: `vehicles-db`).
*   `AUTH_SECRET` — JWT signing secret (required in production).
*   `PORT` — default `3200`.
*   `NODE_ENV` — `development` | `production` | `test`.
*   `SEQUELIZE_SYNC_ALTER` — `sync({ alter: true })` on start; on by default in development, `false` disables it.
*   `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` — Google sign-in.
*   `DEV_LOGIN` — `true` enables developer sign-in (never in production); `DEV_LOGIN_PASSWORD` sets its shared password (default `password`).

Frontend: use `import.meta.env.DEV` for dev/prod API base URL; `cross-env APP_ENV=development` in npm scripts.

Backend test env (`backend/.env.test`): copy from `backend/.env.test.example`; uses `NODE_ENV=test` and `DB_NAME=vehicles-db-test` (must end in `-test`).

## Dev Ports
*   Frontend Vite: `8082`
*   Backend Express: `3200`
*   CORS origin must match the frontend dev URL.

## Test Commands
*   Root: `npm test` (runs backend + frontend)
*   Backend: `cd backend && npm test` (Jest + supertest)
*   Frontend: `cd frontend && npm test` (Vitest + `@vue/test-utils`)
*   Copy `backend/.env.test.example` → `backend/.env.test` before running backend tests locally.
